# PushApp customer profile payload

Host calls `updateUserProfile` with Starquik's flat shape (only the fields this app has):

```ts
await updateUserProfile({
  name: 'Jane Doe',
  phones: ['+919876543210'],
  email: 'jane@example.com',
  alt_emails: [{ email: 'alt@example.com' }], // optional
})
```

Wire PUT body:

```json
{
  "name": "Jane Doe",
  "phones": [{ "phone": "+919876543210" }],
  "additionalInfo": {
    "email": "jane@example.com",
    "alt_emails": [{ "email": "alt@example.com" }]
  }
}
```

- Host builder: `buildMeheryProfileInfo` — never invents `source` (admin-only). Do not copy Starquik commerce fields (cart_value, order dates, segments).
- SDK: scalar `email` stays in `additionalInfo` (PushApp rejects a top-level `emails` add). `phones` strings normalize to `[{ phone }]`. Name is a plain string.
- Pass `code` / `rmCode` only when the caller already has them; do not invent.

Builders: `buildProfileApiPayload` in `profileSnapshotCompare.ts`; host `buildMeheryProfileInfo` in `buildMeheryProfileInfo.ts`.
